  "utterances": {
    "O0": "I was working at the boathouse between the bells. Jonah was at the office hatch during the test. I saw him answer the telephone while I held the pressure lever, but I could not hear the caller. Adrian and I had words about work earlier; I left him standing at his desk.",
    "M-S": "After the first bell and before the second, Ruth brought a grey folder into reception. I was beside the linen table and read forty-one and Bell original on its cover before she wrapped it in a dry cloth and put it on the lower cupboard shelf. I thought she was keeping archive papers dry.",
    "J-C": "Adrian called the office on the direct chart-room house line while Owen was testing the pump. I answered at the hatch and checked the office clock: twenty thirty-six. He asked us to collect the archive box after his meeting and said the Bell original was still sealed on his desk. Near the end I heard him say, Come in, Ruth, and a voice I recognized as Ruth answer, I came for the original, Adrian. I wrote the collection instruction and the call interval in the watchbook. I did not see into the chart room.",
    "R-F": "I collected that folder at our earlier tea visit, before the first bell. I put it in the cupboard later to keep it dry; I did not collect it during the interval between the bells.",
    "I-F": "I walked to the glazed door. He looked up and raised a hand to me from the desk; the white band on the grey folder had a large forty-one on it. I returned to the sheltered bench. Later I saw Ruth's face under the porch lamp as she came through that door with a grey edge under her shawl. I did not read a number on what she carried. From the bench I could see the threshold, not the desk or the inner doorway behind the chart rack."
  },
